cdex (0.0.1-3cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * debian/control: bump Standards-Version to 4.7.4 and drop the
    Priority field, which just spelled out the default.
  * debian/copyright: document the actual per-component licensing of
    the vendored ReactOS tree, its bundled third-party libraries under
    sdk/lib/3rdparty, wallpapers, and fonts, instead of the previous
    blanket GPL-2.0+ claim.
  * runtime/bin: drop the .sh extension from cdex-registry, matching
    every other script, and normalize shebangs to #!/bin/bash /
    #!/usr/bin/python3 throughout.

 -- Evgeny Golyshev <eugulixes@cusdeb.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:07:47 +0300

cdex (0.0.1-2cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * debian/control: use a dedicated Section, matching the convention of
    other desktop environments (GNOME, KDE, Xfce).
  * debian/control: sort and align Depends/Build-Depends.
  * debian/control: rewrite package descriptions.
  * Reorganize package layout: move runtime files under runtime/
    (bin/config/themes/icons split), rename reactos-src/ to src/,
    normalize utility names to a single cdex- prefix, and fix the
    Makefile's stale fontconfig install path.

